# Supabase
.branches
.temp

# Local developer seed — recreates the dev account after `supabase db reset`.
#
# NEVER COMMIT THIS. It holds a real email address and a real bcrypt password hash. A hash is not
# plaintext, but it is still a credential: in a repo it can be brute-forced offline, at leisure,
# with no rate limit and no lockout. It is also machine-specific — it recreates ONE person's local
# account and would be meaningless, or actively confusing, on anyone else's checkout.
#
# See supabase/seed.sql.example for the shape, and the header of seed.sql for how to regenerate it.
seed.sql

# dotenvx
.env.keys
.env.local
.env.*.local
